        "completedSourceTexts": [
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-sichuan-leshan-zigong-yibin-2025-m2:36",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-sichuan-leshan-zigong-yibin-2025-m2:seven-choices:2",
            "text": "Lack of motivation can be the biggest obstacle to reaching your goals. Consider why you are struggling, when you have no motivation to complete a task (or even start one). Then, develop a plan to help motivate yourself to get going."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-sichuan-leshan-zigong-yibin-2025-m2:37",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-sichuan-leshan-zigong-yibin-2025-m2:seven-choices:3",
            "text": "Reward yourself for working. Create a small reward for yourself that you can earn for your hard work. Focus on the reward to keep your motivation alive. Consider whether you are likely to be more motivated by smaller, more frequent rewards or a bigger reward for a complete job. You may want to experiment with a few different strategies until you discover an approach that works best for you."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-sichuan-leshan-zigong-yibin-2025-m2:38",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-sichuan-leshan-zigong-yibin-2025-m2:seven-choices:4",
            "text": "Act as if you feel motivated. You can trick yourself into feeling motivated by changing your behavior. For example, rather than sit on the couch all day waiting for motivation to strike, get dressed and get moving. Your action will increase your motivation, which makes it easier to keep going."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-sichuan-leshan-zigong-yibin-2025-m2:39",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-sichuan-leshan-zigong-yibin-2025-m2:seven-choices:5",
            "text": "Argue the opposite. Struggling with motivation, you’ll likely come up with reasons why you shouldn’t take any action. These will keep you stuck. Instead, argue all the reasons why you might succeed. Arguing the opposite can help you see both sides of the coin. It can also remind you that an overly pessimistic outcome isn’t completely accurate. There’s a chance that things might work out better than you expect."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-sichuan-leshan-zigong-yibin-2025-m2:40",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-sichuan-leshan-zigong-yibin-2025-m2:seven-choices:6",
            "text": "Manage your to-do list. It’s tough to feel motivated when your to-do list is overwhelming. Take a look at your list, and determine if it’s too long. If so, get rid of tasks that aren’t essential. Prioritize the most important things, and move those to the top. You might find a slight change in your to-do list – or the way you view your to-do list – will help you to see your tasks as more manageable. Eventually, you feel more driven to move on."
          }
        ],
